WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 1.4 · Strategic Foundations
Values in practice

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Values set early shape the culture of everything you build.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:26.652
Values are the principles that guide what you do when decisions are hard. A single word is only a start: describe what people will actually do, and how you would notice it.

4
00:00:27.052 --> 00:00:27.652
Each value in three lines

5
00:00:27.652 --> 00:00:37.500
What it means: One sentence on what the value means for you. For example: Inclusion: anyone in our neighbourhood can take part, whatever their income or ability.

6
00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:49.200
How it shows: What you will actually do, and what it costs in time and money. For example: We budget for step-free access and run one session a month in the evening.

7
00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:59.878
What you avoid: The behaviour the value rules out, even under pressure. For example: We never set a fee that keeps out families on low incomes.

8
00:01:00.278 --> 00:01:00.878
Why they matter

9
00:01:00.878 --> 00:01:06.181
1. They guide you when there is no rule to follow.

10
00:01:06.181 --> 00:01:11.485
2. Values set early shape the culture of everything you build.

11
00:01:11.485 --> 00:01:17.789
3. Agreeing them now prevents conflict at your first hard decision.

12
00:01:18.189 --> 00:01:18.789
What they guide

13
00:01:18.789 --> 00:01:24.093
1. How you handle difficult decisions you can foresee this year.

14
00:01:24.093 --> 00:01:29.396
2. Your first budget, because practising values costs time and money.

15
00:01:29.396 --> 00:01:34.959
3. Your code of conduct, later in the course.

16
00:01:35.359 --> 00:01:35.959
What to avoid

17
00:01:35.959 --> 00:01:40.522
Adopting values only because other organisations display them.

18
00:01:40.522 --> 00:01:45.456
Too many: keep three to five you can practise.

19
00:01:45.456 --> 00:01:51.019
Ignoring trade-offs, such as openness against participants’ privacy.

20
00:01:51.619 --> 00:01:53.419
You write three to five values and test them on a hard decision.

21
00:01:53.419 --> 00:01:57.419
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

22
00:01:58.919 --> 00:02:02.019
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
